WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.464
Today’s lesson goal: Today’s lesson goal: store many values in lists. Look up data with dictionaries. Choose the right collection for the job.

2
00:00:11.314 --> 00:00:26.266
Lists: ordered collections: Lists are ordered collections. Keep items in order and access by index. Append, remove, and loop through items. Great for playlists, baskets, and queues.

3
00:00:27.116 --> 00:00:39.260
Dictionaries: keys to values: Dictionaries map a key to a value — like a labelled folder. Use them for fast lookups such as name to email or id to score. Keys must be unique.

4
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:50.310
Worked example: contacts: Worked example: keep a list of friend names and a dictionary of name to phone number. Loop the list and print each number from the dictionary.

5
00:00:51.160 --> 00:01:04.288
Common mistakes: Common mistakes: off-by-one index errors. Assuming a key exists without checking — use get or check first. Mixing up list order with dictionary keys.

6
00:01:05.138 --> 00:01:18.410
Practice checkpoint: Practice checkpoint: build a tiny shopping list or contact book. Add, print, and look up one item. Then continue in the written Module 5 lesson and quiz.
